  "details": "SDK Version: it's present right now in 2021.09.03.09.25, both 2 and 3 (both avatar and world), but it's not a new issue - it's been in SDKs for over a year now.\n\nDescription:\n2 shaders - Bumped Specular and Bumped Mapped Specular - appear under the same name (Bumped Mapped Specular) in Unity when trying to pick a shader for a material.\nWhen you pick either of them, they both appear as marked (pic attached).\nIronically, despite that they both appear as Bumped Mapped Specular, when you use them, you're actually using the Bumped Specular one.\n(in Unity 2018 they appeared as a single position instead of 2 separate ones with the same name, looks like in 2019 they stopped removing duplicates)\n\nSteps to reproduce: Create a Unity project, import any of the SDKs, create a material, click the shader selection, go to VRChat/Mobile and there you'll see it.\n\nSteps to fix:\nOpen the file Assets/VRCSDK/Sample Assets/Shaders/Mobile/VRChat-Mobile-BumpedSpecular.shader\nand change line\nShader \"VRChat/Mobile/Bumped Mapped Specular\"\nto\nShader \"VRChat/Mobile/Bumped Specular\"\nand that's it.\n\ncheers\n\nPS: i don't understand why one is called \"Mapped\" and the other not, given that the only difference between them is the additional Specular Color in the \"Mapped\" one, and not any kind of map.",
